WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.180
Sakuragi Institute’s research fellows,
Satoshi and Go,

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.980
headed to Galar to investigate
the mysteries of Daimax.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.570
They were separated in the Slumbering Weald,
and each met a mysterious Pokémon.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.830
Meanwhile, Pokémon began Daimaxing on their own and rampaging.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.580
Satoshi worked with Dande
to stop their rampages,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.380
while Go went with Sonia
to try and solve the legend of the hero.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:35.010
At the same time, Rose was attempting to
revive the Pokémon which once nearly wiped out Galar.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.640
What is his goal?

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:43.710
Then, when Go and Sonia were investigating a mural,
they were attacked by a mysterious group.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.070
Impossible!
There were statues behind the mural?!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.830
Two humans,
and two Pokemon?

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.810
Those Pokemon...

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:33.800
Hey! You can talk
all you want later!

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.180
Knock them all down
with Dai Steel!

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.400
Rabbifoot! Are you okay?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.990
All right! Dai Knuckle!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.450
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.440
Finish them with Kyodai Stench!

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.320
<i>We’ll</i> finish <i>you</i> first!
Rabbifoot, Dai Burn!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.620
How’s that?
Want some more?

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.900
You’ll regret this!

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.870
Go, that was great!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.770
Guess it went well for being
my first Daimax battle.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.080
Rabbifoot, good job!

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.220
You really are my Pokémon!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.240
Oh, right! The statues!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:09.230
Now then, time to meet up
with Go in Lateral Town!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.920
Go for it, Kairyu!

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.320
Galar itself is what
let me reach my current life.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.240
And I intend to do everything
within my power,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.580
in order for this marvelous view
to last a thousand years.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.800
A thousand years...

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.020
I can’t even imagine
that far ahead!

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.360
When I was in the Slumbering Weald,

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.110
I met a Pokemon that
looked a lot like this statue.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.930
Though it didn’t have
the sword and shield...

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.560
When I tried to catch it,
my Monster Ball went through it,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.190
and the fog got worse...

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.380
I fell asleep out of nowhere...

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.610
Is that why it’s called
the Slumbering Weald?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.050
And then?

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.100
When I woke up,
the Pokemon was gone.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.620
What a bizarre experience.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.700
What’s this?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.200
It looks like their names...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:19.090
It says the one holding the sword is Zacian,
and the one with the shield is Zamazenta.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.870
Now we know for sure!

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.480
The legendary hero
wasn’t one person, but two!

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.580
And they both
had a Pokemon with them.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:30.390
Which were Zacian and Zamazenta!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.380
The black vortex that once covered the sky
was a Pokémon called Black Night.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.630
It nearly wiped out Galar.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:47.860
But the two heroes, and their partners
Zacian and Zamazenta quelled the calamity.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.110
Yes, that about summarizes it.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.810
Okay, there they are!

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.790
Catch them this time!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.810
Those guys again?

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.250
They don’t give up...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.690
What do we do?

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.460
Times like these...

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.970
...you gotta bowl straight through ‘em!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.930
Where to?

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.320
The Slumbering Weald!

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.860
To do what exactly?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.210
If the legendary heroes
really quelled Black Night,

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.490
Zacian and Zamazenta
might lend us their help!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.450
Okay!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.620
Oh, come on...!

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.670
Go, hold on tight!

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.750
Hey! After them!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.470
Sir!

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:56.480
M-Mr. Dande! You can’t go through here
without Chairman Rose’s permission!

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.850
Chairman Rose called me here.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:02.470
Okay, I’ll confirm it with him,
so please wait outside the elevator.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.660
Sorry, but I don’t have time.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.570
Go?

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.240
Satoshi, where are you?

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.610
On the way to Lateral Town.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.200
Sorry, we aren’t there anymore.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:19.750
Huh?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.310
Kairyu, stop!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.110
Hey, Satoshi...

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.430
When we got split up
in the Slumbering Weald,

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.630
did you happen to meet
a strange Pokémon?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:30.850
I did, I did!

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.010
How did you know that?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.930
I saw one too.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.570
It looked like this?

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.850
Yeah, just like that!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.390
Their names are
Zacian and Zamazenta.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.440
Zacian? Zamazenta?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.610
Those Pokémon are linked with
the legend of the hero.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.290
The legend of the hero?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.360
Yeah.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.650
The black vortex was Black Night,
a Pokémon.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:08:00.030
And it was quelled by Zacian, Zamazenta
and two heroes.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.830
At least, that’s our deduction.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:06.020
Black Night... Two heroes?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.720
And right now, Pokémon are
Daimaxing on their own and rampaging, yeah?

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:18.560
If our deduction is right,
that’s because of Black Night.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:23.230
Which means it might’ve been
revived somewhere.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.430
The way things are going,
Galar is headed for the brink of destruction again.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.470
Quick! Stop the injection
of Galar particles!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.240
We won’t make it in time!

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.490
What the...

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.880
It’s overloading!

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:00.640
What’s wrong?

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.640
There’s this red light...!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.410
Where’s it coming from?

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:08.260
Uhh... Rotom, where is that?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.980
Knuckle City.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.360
Black Night might be there, then.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.100
If Pokémon are exposed to that light,
they’ll start rampaging again!

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.280
I have to do something, Go!

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.340
Got it! I’ll go search for
Zacian and Zamazenta!

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.510
Let’s talk later!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:26.510
Okay!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.300
Kairyu, let’s go!

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.500
So this was the light that was
making Pokémon rampage?

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.320
If we don’t do something,
Mugendaina’s going to escape the hangar.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.940
Mugendaina?

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.360
Contact Chairman Rose!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.230
Understood.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:51.980
I knew it.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:02.560
It’s finally happening!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.840
Hurry on out,
strongest and evilest Pokémon!

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.570
We’re gonna catch you, meow!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.880
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.180
No way!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:34.570
This is... Mugendaina?

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.000
Pocket Monsters.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.380
You still can’t get in touch
with Chairman Rose?!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:00.010
What are you doing?!
It’s going to get out to the surface!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.120
Mr. Dande?!
Why are <i>you</i> here?!

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:06.340
It doesn’t matter!
Don’t you have any way of stopping it?!

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:11.720
But... Anything related to Mugendaina,
we need to confirm with Chairman Rose...

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.400
Let’s go, Lizardon!

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.310
That was awful, meow.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.040
What’s that?

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.370
We gotta get outta here, meow!

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.880
Hold it!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.670
Our <i>prey</i> just came straight to <i>us!</i>

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.280
We’ll catch it here!

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:39.480
Yeah!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.070
Team Rocket is on the scene!

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.960
Nyarth, do it!

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.310
You got it, meow!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.220
Huh?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.240
Nyarth?

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:12.620
That’s perfect!
Go catch that strongest and evilest Pokemon!

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:15.570
Nyarth?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:24.720
Hey! What’d you do that for?!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.270
Team Rocket?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.820
What are you doing here?

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.520
The brat boy?!

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:42.700
Nyarth?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.090
This weird light hit him
and he went crazy!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:48.180
The strongest and evilest
Pokémon’s to blame!

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.010
Go do something about it!

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.000
He’s here!

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.260
It really... was in here...

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:59.250
Zacian! Zamazenta!

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.100
Show yourselves!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.380
The fog!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.070
It’s just like before.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:14.770
Pokémon are involuntarily Daimaxing and
going on destructive rampages all over Galar once again!

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:19.270
Satoshi?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:24.530
The red lights that trigger the rampages
are being fired out of Knuckle City Stadium–

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.620
That’s Black Night?

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.990
It really was revived!

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.320
We need to hurry and
find Zacian and Zamazenta.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:37.490
Come on! Zacian! Zamazenta!

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:39.420
Black Night has been revived!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:43.140
Galar is going to be wiped out
if we don’t do something! Please!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.920
Come on out again!

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:58.820
Zacian... Zamazenta...?

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:00.690
You showed up!

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:05.690
Hold on!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.860
We need your help!

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:18.780
They vanished...

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.780
Rabbifoot?!

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.870
I never knew this was here...

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.730
A sword and shield...

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:44.310
The sword and shield
from the legend?

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.620
Yeah, they must be.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.070
That’s... Black Night?

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.580
Dodge it!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.750
Kairyu!

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:03.950
Are you okay?

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.730
Have a rest.

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.620
Mr. Dande!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:13.850
Satoshi!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.820
That’s Black Night, isn’t it?

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:20.340
Correct!

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:25.480
The people who once feared it
named it so.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.230
Chairman Rose!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:32.240
But I lovingly renamed it
Mugendaina— “Infinite”!

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:38.250
After all, it’s a valuable Pokémon
which creates infinite energy.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:42.670
The enormous power it’s displaying
is even beyond my expectations.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:51.450
I never knew the audience safety barrier
could help in such a way.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:57.700
Dande. We’ve often discussed
the future of Galar together.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.890
Now’s not the time!

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:04.400
No, this is all for Galar’s future!

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.400
What do you mean?

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:11.890
I found that in the near future,
Galar’s energy will be exhausted.

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:16.250
I racked my brains on
how I could solve this issue,

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:20.660
and discovered Galar particles
could serve as a new energy source.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.410
Galar particles?

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:26.100
Yes. And more than that...

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:31.920
I learned Mugendaina was the Pokémon of my dreams,
infinitely creating Galar particles!

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:37.300
But those beams cause Pokémon to
Daimax and go on rampages!

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.320
It’s very troubling.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:44.580
That’s why I’ve guided
talented trainers like you.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:52.280
Yes... You shall catch
the revived Mugendaina, and control it!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.880
As I desire!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.970
What’re you doing?

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:02.880
If the sword and shield
belong to Zacian and Zamazenta,

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:05.340
they may have some hidden powers.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:06.440
I get it.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:09.670
Maybe they can help us
stop Black Night.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.810
Let’s hurry to Knuckle City!

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:12.560
Yes!

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:16.930
My father, he worked in the mines.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.380
He worked day and night,

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:22.630
to extract the energy source
we once used,

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.180
and to support our family.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.420
But after an unforeseen accident,
he never came back.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.260
But what do you think?

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.680
As long as we have Mugendaina,

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:37.080
nobody will ever need
to suffer as I did,

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.540
and we’ll have infinite energy.

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.330
See...

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:45.460
I’m thinking of the Galar
a thousand years from now!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.160
Dande...

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:52.120
I’ve watched over you and nurtured you
since you were young, all for this very moment.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:55.090
You can’t turn me down now.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:57.220
I’ll catch Mugendaina.

00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.810
You’ll be a true hero of Galar!

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:03.220
But... only to calm it down.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.480
It’s already caused immense damage!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.230
I don’t want to witness
any further tragedies!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:11.360
How naïve you are.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:32.960
It looks like Mugendaina’s
full revival is near.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:36.590
Go on, Dande! You’re up!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:41.600
Even if it creates Galar particles,
Mugendaina is too dangerous!

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:45.340
I’ll catch it, and seal it away!

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.330
Satoshi, let’s go.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:48.850
Right!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:49.980
Stop!

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:52.650
You’ve disappointed me.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.900
Daioudou! Power Whip!

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.910
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.170
Satoshi?

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:11.460
Mr. Dande,
please go catch Mugendaina!

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.350
Got it.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:21.400
You intend to make all of my effort
be for naught?

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.800
I won’t let you cause any more
innocent Pokemon to rampage!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.640
What insolence.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.560
Nutrey!

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.690
Lend me your help, Riolu!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.010
How long’s he gonna keep rampaging?!

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:46.140
Just go back to normal already!

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.080
We’re nearly at the stadium!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.720
What do we do?

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.880
Times like these...
you gotta <i>go</i> straight through ‘em!

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:58.620
Get moving, Go!

00:19:58.620 --> 00:19:59.300
But...

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.810
I’ll be fine.
Get in there and help Satoshi!

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:03.680
Right.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.220
Rabbifoot, let’s go!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:11.480
I’ll be your opponent.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.480
You wanna be crushed?!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.030
What’s all the noise?

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.190
I can’t let you trouble a beautiful lady.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:36.920
Not on the home turf of the mighty Kibana,
Dragon-type Gym Leader.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:49.700
Oh, it’s you.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:53.390
That boy playing at solving riddles
with Magnolia’s granddaughter.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.230
Something wrong with that?

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.930
This will not do at all.

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:00.400
I cannot have you
disturbing Chairman Rose.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:04.860
I’m just here to stop Black Night
threatening Galar—

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:06.920
That’s disturbing him!

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.610
Black Night...
No, Mugendaina.

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:17.880
How much time and money do you think
Chairman Rose has spent to revive it?

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:22.130
So you were the ones
trying to catch us!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:26.060
